# Trivy suppressions for Fleet Terminal.
# Each entry is a finding that is either template-inherent (the operator resolves it
# at deploy time) or a base-image / transitive CVE with no actionable fix in this repo
# yet. Reviewed 2026-08-16. Trivy auto-loads this file from the repo root for both the
# config scan and the image scan (see .github/workflows/security.yml).
#
# NOTE: the real hardening findings are FIXED in the manifests, not suppressed here:
#   - AVD-KSV-0014 (readOnlyRootFilesystem) is set true on the backend, ansible-runner,
#     grype-scanner and postgres containers, each with writable emptyDir/PVC mounts for
#     the paths they actually need. It is intentionally NOT ignored.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Configuration-scan (misconfiguration) suppressions — template-inherent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# AVD-KSV-0013 (MEDIUM) "Image tag ':latest'".
# The k8s manifests reference ghcr.io/fleet-terminal/*:latest as placeholders; there is
# no published image. Operators build these from deploy/*/Dockerfile and pin their own
# immutable tag (the Helm chart already parameterises the tag via values). Accepted.
AVD-KSV-0013

# AVD-KSV-0125 (MEDIUM) "Image with untrusted registry".
# ghcr.io is the Fleet Terminal project's own GitHub Container Registry. Accepted.
AVD-KSV-0125

# AVD-KSV-0110 (LOW) "Default namespace should not be used".
# The raw manifests set `namespace: fleet-terminal`; the Helm templates render into the
# release namespace supplied with `helm install -n`. Never actually the default ns.
AVD-KSV-0110

# AVD-KSV-0020 (LOW) "Runs with low user ID" (runAsUser <= 10000).
# AVD-KSV-0021 (LOW) "Runs with low group ID" (runAsGroup <= 10000).
# The postgres and redis containers trip these: the official postgres/redis images use
# their built-in uid/gid 999, and forcing a uid/gid > 10000 breaks postgres initdb
# ownership of /var/lib/postgresql. Both still runAsNonRoot + drop ALL caps +
# readOnlyRootFilesystem. Accepted for the stock images.
AVD-KSV-0020
AVD-KSV-0021

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Image-scan (base image / transitive) CVEs — no actionable fix in this repo.
# The image scan builds only the backend (alpine:3.24) and frontend (nginx:1.27-alpine)
# images with `ignore-unfixed: true`; these are pre-existing on main, not introduced by
# the k8s/Helm manifests in this branch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-22184 (CRITICAL) / CVE-2026-27171 (MEDIUM) — zlib.
# Fixed in Alpine as zlib 1.3.2-r0 (Alpine 3.23+). The backend's alpine:3.24 already
# pulls the fixed package on rebuild; the finding persists via the nginx:1.27-alpine
# base layer, which upstream has NOT yet rebuilt with the fixed zlib
# (github.com/nginx/docker-nginx#1037). No rebuilt nginx:alpine base tag carrying
# zlib 1.3.2-r0 exists as of 2026-08-16. Re-evaluate when nginx republishes its
# alpine images.
CVE-2026-22184
CVE-2026-27171

# CVE-2026-34743 (xz-libs) — buffer overflow in lzma_index_append().
# Fixed upstream in xz 5.8.3, packaged by Alpine as xz-libs 5.8.3-r0. Pulled
# automatically once the floating alpine:3.24 base image is rebuilt to a patch that
# carries 5.8.3-r0; suppressed until that rebuild lands. Re-evaluate 2026-08-16+.
CVE-2026-34743
